WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.550
- Joining us from Glasgow,

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.739
please welcome Sam Heughan, everybody.

00:00:03.739 --> 00:00:06.489
(crowd cheering)

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:08.533
Oh, my God.

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:09.366
What's up, Sam?

00:00:09.366 --> 00:00:11.950
Those were some nice moves
and a nice kilt, man.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.461
- Oh, Kelly, I can't
believe you showed that one.

00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:16.294
(crowd laughing)

00:00:16.294 --> 00:00:17.490
C'mon.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.280
- That's why it's amazing.
- I know.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.570
- Is a kilt your usual attire?

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.790
- I mean, it's not really.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.330
Obviously, in the show, Men In Kilts,

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.750
we do wear a lot of kilts.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.550
And just for you, Kelly,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.440
the director of your show wanted me

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.780
to show them what I was
wearing, but I refused,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.700
I wanted to save this for you.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.478
But I wore this, especially for you.

00:00:36.478 --> 00:00:37.311
- Yeah!

00:00:38.244 --> 00:00:39.639
Woo!

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.791
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:42.900
(crowd cheering and laughing)

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:46.420
I'm just saying, a real man
wears a kilt and owns it.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.503
That's a real man.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:49.780
I know what a family tartan is,

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.430
but I know a lot of people might not.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.900
What is that?

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.410
- Yeah, I mean, it's
traditionally every family,

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.140
every clan has their own tartan,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.070
and it dates back kind of
to the Victorian times.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.730
Before that point, there
were tartans associated

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.880
with different clans, different
motto, different houses.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.860
But yeah, it was made more traditional

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.223
in the Victorian times.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.580
We wear a variety of kilts
and tartans in the show.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.310
And this one I was
wearing today, actually,

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.660
is the Outlander tartan.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.278
- Oh, that's so cool.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:22.720
Have you ever accidentally
flashed someone in your kilt?

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.540
And, but by the way, you
probably did it on purpose.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.958
But have you ever accidentally done it?

00:01:25.958 --> 00:01:27.710
(crowd laughing)

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:28.543
- Do you know what?

00:01:28.543 --> 00:01:30.078
I think I almost flashed
you there, actually.

00:01:30.078 --> 00:01:33.200
I didn't mean to, but yeah.
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.880
I mean, not intentionally but you know,

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.060
it's kind of dangerous.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.600
It's a kind of extreme
sport, wearing a kilt.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.850
And in Men In Kilts,
we do a lot of things.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.640
We're riding bicycles, we're abseiling,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.860
you guys call it repelling.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.700
We're hiking, we're doing
all kinds of sports in kilts.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.750
So I'm sure at some point,
if you look closely,

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.740
you might see something
you don't wanna see.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:55.573
- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:56.783
Or maybe they do?

